  (text "F1: Fuse 1A/63V slow-blow (Littelfuse 0452001.MRL or equiv.)\nD1: Schottky reverse-polarity P-channel MOSFET + gate resistor (Si2333DS)\nTV1: TVS bidirectional 60V/600W (SMAJ60A or P6KE60A)\nC1,C2: 100uF/63V electrolytic (bulk), C3: 10uF/63V MLCC\nL1: 10uH/2A common-mode choke (TDK ACM2520-201-2P-T)"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 44 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0003-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "Net: 48V_IN+ -> F1 -> TVS clamp node -> D1 drain -> 48V_FILT+\nNet: 48V_IN- -> PGND\nAll components rated >= 60V; TVS clamped to 60V for transient protection up to 60V.\nSELV class: 48V DC, normal range 43.2-52.8V."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 60 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0004-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 2: 4-SWITCH SYNCHRONOUS BUCK-BOOST (44V LED BUS) ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 82 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0005-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "Controller: LT8390A (Analog Devices) – 4-switch synchronous buck-boost controller\n  - Input range: 6V to 60V; Output range: 1V to 60V\n  - Datasheet: https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt8390a.pdf\nQ1,Q2: High-side/low-side buck switches  – AON7534 N-ch 30V 25A (or Si7336ADP)\nQ3,Q4: High-side/low-side boost switches – AON6424 N-ch 40V 20A (or Si7464DP)\nL2: 47uH/3A shielded power inductor (Bourns SRR1260-470M or TDK SLF12565T-470M3R0-PF)\nC4-C6: 47uF/63V electrolytic output, C7: 100nF ceramic bypass\nR_CS_H, R_CS_L: 10mohm/1% current sense (Vishay WSBS2515R0100FEA)\nITH/SS/RT/FCB pins connected per LT8390A datasheet typical application.\nSW node: switching frequency ~200kHz (set by RT resistor to GND)\nOutput: LED_BUS+ nominally 44V, regulated; serves as common LED anode.\nOutput capacitor: 47uF x 2 / 63V electrolytic + 4.7uF/63V MLCC.\nFeedback network: resistor divider from LED_BUS+ to FB pin of LT8390A.\n  R_FB1 (top): 750k / R_FB2 (bot): 38.3k for 44V output (0.8V ref).\n  Vout = 0.8 x (1 + R_FB1/R_FB2) = 44V\nEnable: tied to 3.3V logic; MCU can shutdown via SHDN pin.\nOVP comparator: internal to LT8390A; external OVP FET optional for hard fault."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 90 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0006-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 3: LINEAR LOW-SIDE CURRENT SINKS (WW and CW) ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 150 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0007-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "Architecture: common LED_BUS+ anode (44V) -> LED string -> low-side N-ch MOSFET sink -> sense resistor -> PGND\nPer channel:\n  Q_WW / Q_CW: NTMFS5C604NL N-ch 60V 15A MOSFET (SOT-223 or TO-252)\n    Gate driven by op-amp error amplifier: compares Vsense with DAC setpoint\n  R_SENSE_WW / R_SENSE_CW: 0.1 ohm / 1W (Vishay WSHM2818R1000FEB)\n    100mohm: at 700mA -> 70mV sense voltage; at 400mA -> 40mV; at 1mA -> 0.1mV\n  U_CS_WW / U_CS_CW: OPA2333 (TI) precision rail-to-rail op-amp\n    Configured as integrating error amplifier: \n      non-inv (+): DAC output (MCU DAC or I2C DAC, 0-1.0V range)\n      inv (-):     Vsense from Kelvin sense resistor tap\n      output:      Gate of Q_WW/Q_CW via 47R gate resistor\n    Compensation: 10nF/10k RC at op-amp output for loop stability\n  Soft-start: MCU ramps DAC output from 0V, enforcing dV/dt limit\n  Current limit: hardware OCP comparator (LM393) monitors Vsense;\n    if Vsense > 105mV (OCP = ~1.05A) the comparator drives gate to 0V via NAND latch\n    OCP latch is reset by MCU GPIO after fault clearance\n  Default state: DAC output = 0V on power-up -> gate = 0V -> channel OFF (fail-safe)\n  Enable: MCU GPIO controls DAC output enable; independent per channel\n  Dimming: analog DAC control provides linear current 0.1mA - 700mA\n    0.1% at 700mA full scale -> min DAC code corresponds to ~0.7mA\n    For lower currents, 16-bit external I2C DAC (MCP4728) provides resolution\n  Thermal note: Pdiss_max per channel = (V_BUS - V_LED) * I_LED\n    Worst case: (44 - 28) * 0.7 = 11.2W per sink\n    Both channels: max 22.4W dissipation in current sinks + switching losses\n    Thermal vias to Al enclosure REQUIRED; see thermal design note.\nJ3: LED+/WW-/CW- screw terminal (5.08mm, rated 16A per pin)\nTest point TP_SENSE_WW, TP_SENSE_CW: Kelvin-routed 0.5mm test pads"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 157 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0008-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 4: AUXILIARY POWER SUPPLY (48V -> 5V -> 3.3V) ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 235 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0009-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "Stage 1: 48V -> 5V isolated flyback or non-isolated buck\n  U_AUX1: VIPer26HDTR (ST Microelectronics) – integrated offline/48V flyback controller\n    Or: LMR14020SDDA (TI) – 42V input synchronous buck for 5V/2A\n    Datasheet LMR14020: https://www.ti.com/product/LMR14020\n  L_AUX: 47uH/1A (Wurth 744771147)\n  Output: 5V / 500mA (powers MCU, DAC, DALI isolated side)\nStage 2: 5V -> 3.3V LDO\n  U_LDO: AP2112K-3.3 (Diodes Inc) LDO 3.3V/600mA\n  C_LDO_IN: 10uF/10V; C_LDO_OUT: 22uF/6.3V\n  Output: 3.3V_MCU for MCU core, flash, I2C DAC, sense amp supply\nNet naming: 5V_AUX (intermediate), 3.3V_MCU (MCU rail)\nProtection: ferrite bead FB1 on 5V to DALI isolated side supply"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 242 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0010-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 5: MCU, NVM, SWD, STATUS ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 295 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0011-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "MCU: STM32G031K8T6 (ST Microelectronics) – ARM Cortex-M0+ 64MHz 64KB flash 8KB SRAM\n  Package: LQFP-32 (7mm x 7mm)\n  Datasheet: https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/stm32g031k8.pdf\n  Peripherals used:\n    USART1: DALI half-duplex receive via optocoupler\n    TIM1/TIM2: DALI bit timing, PWM generation (ultrasonic >40kHz for enable only)\n    DAC1 CH1/CH2: Analog current setpoint output for WW/CW sinks (12-bit)\n    I2C1: External 16-bit DAC (MCP4728) for fine-grained sub-1% control\n    ADC1: NTC temperature sense, bus voltage monitoring, LED bus voltage\n    GPIO: OCP latch reset, enable lines, LED status, fault indication\n    SWD: PA13/PA14 for programming/debug\n    NRST: Hardware reset pin\nNVM: AT24C32E (Microchip) I2C EEPROM 32Kbit (4KB)\n  Purpose: stores DALI address, groups, scenes (16), last dim/CCT state, fault log\n  Write-cycle limit: 1M cycles; firmware uses wear-leveling for dim/CCT state\n  Address: 0x50 on I2C1\nXTAL: 32.768kHz backup crystal (Abracon ABS07-120-32.768kHz-T) optional\nStatus LEDs: LED_STATUS (green, PB3), LED_FAULT (red, PB4) via 1k series resistors\nSWD connector: J4 – 4-pin 1.27mm pitch (GND, SWDCLK, SWDIO, 3.3V)\n  Also: BOOT0 solder jumper SJ1 for DFU mode\n  Test points: TP_SWDIO, TP_SWDCLK, TP_NRST, TP_GND\nReset: RC filter on NRST, 100nF to GND\n3.3V_MCU rail: 100nF + 10uF decoupling per VDD pin\nAnalog supply: VDDA tied to 3.3V_MCU through 1uH bead + 1uF/100nF"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 302 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0012-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 6: GALVANICALLY ISOLATED DALI INTERFACE ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 383 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0013-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "Isolation goal: 2.5kVrms component class (subject to final safety standard review)\nIsolation architecture:\n  TX path: MCU GPIO -> IS181XBHTR (IXYS) DALI optocoupler TX (integrated DALI driver)\n    Or: SFH6156-4 (Osram) fast optocoupler + discrete DALI bus driver\n  RX path: Bus line -> voltage divider (15V clamp) -> SFH6156-4 receiver -> MCU GPIO\n  DALI bus driver: active pull-down MOSFET (BSS138) with 200ohm series resistor\n    DALI bus sourced from isolated 5V_DALI supply (derived from 5V_AUX via flyback coupling)\nAlternative integrated approach:\n  U_DALI: NXP UBA2015 DALI slave controller IC (handles Manchester encode/decode)\n    Interfaces to MCU via UART; eliminates need for custom DALI bit-bang firmware\n    Datasheet: https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/UBA2015.pdf\n  NOTE: UBA2015 may simplify certification path; firmware interface described in firmware-interface.md\nESD protection:\n  D_ESD1/D2: PRTR5V0U2X (NXP) dual-channel ESD protection on DALI_A/DALI_B lines\n  TVS_DALI: P4SMA16A 16V unidirectional TVS between DALI_A and DALI_B\nPhysical isolation barrier:\n  PCB keepout: no copper, no vias, no components in a 8mm band between DALI and non-isolated domains\n  Minimum creepage/clearance: 8mm (designed for 48V SELV + 2.5kV isolation goal)\n  Final spacing subject to IEC 62368-1 / EN 61347-1 safety assessment\nConnector J2: DALI_A / DALI_B – 2-pin 5.08mm screw terminal\nTest points: TP_DALI_A, TP_DALI_B (on isolated side)"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 390 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0014-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== BLOCK 7: NTC TEMPERATURE SENSING ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 458 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0015-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "NTC1: Vishay NTCLE100E3104JB0 100k NTC thermistor\n  Location: thermally coupled to current sink MOSFET heatsink region / PCB bottom copper\n  Or: dedicated NTC connector J_NTC (2-pin JST PH2.0) for external mounting on Al enclosure\nCircuit: voltage divider from 3.3V_MCU:\n  R_NTC_PULL: 100k 1% resistor to 3.3V -> divider node -> NTC -> GND\n  ADC input: MCU PA0/ADC1_IN0 reads V_NTC\n  Firmware calculates temperature via Steinhart-Hart or lookup table\nOVERTEMP thresholds (firmware-configurable):\n  Warning: 70°C -> reduce max current by 20%\n  Shutdown: 85°C -> turn off both current sinks, set fault flag\n  Hysteresis: 10°C for re-enable\nInput voltage monitoring:\n  V_BUS sense: resistor divider R_VIN1 (750k) / R_VIN2 (38.3k) -> MCU ADC\n  Monitors 48V input for UVLO (<43V) and OVP (>55V) conditions\nLED bus voltage monitoring:\n  V_LED_BUS sense: resistor divider R_VBUS1 (750k) / R_VBUS2 (38.3k) -> MCU ADC\n  Used for closed-loop power calculation: P_LED = V_LED_BUS * (I_WW + I_CW)"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 30 464 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0016-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

  (text "=== POWER BUDGET SUMMARY ==="
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 120 30 0)
    (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0017-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "LED output (max):  WW 700mA x 40V = 28W  OR  CW 700mA x 40V = 28W  (firmware limits total to 30W)\nBuck-boost loss:   ~5% at full load -> +1.5W\nCurrent sink loss: (44V - LED_Vf) * I_LED e.g. (44-36)*0.7 = 5.6W per channel\nAux supply:        ~2W\nTotal input power: ~38W typical at 30W LED output (efficiency ~79%)\nInput current:     38W / 43.2V = 880mA max -> PCB traces and fuse rated 1.5A"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 120 38 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "cccccccc-0018-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )

